.TH MKDIR 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkdir \- make directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR mode ]
.I dir
.RI [ dir ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkdir
creates the directories named by the
.I dir
operands, in the order given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " mode"
Set the file permission bits of each newly-created directory to
.IR mode ,
using the same
.I mode
grammar as
.BR chmod (1).
In symbolic-mode strings, the
.B +
and
.B \-
operators are interpreted relative to an assumed initial mode of
.BR a=rwx .
.TP
.B \-p
Create any missing intermediate pathname components. It is not an
error for a named directory to already exist when
.B \-p
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-
Marks the end of options; every remaining argument is treated as a
.I dir
operand, even one that begins with
.BR \- .
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I dir
A pathname of a directory to be created.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All the specified directories were created successfully (or,
with
.BR \-p ,
already existed).
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred; processing continues with the next operand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chmod (1),
.BR rmdir (1),
.BR rm (1)
